# radiantsmiles client-site build — repo-local ignores.
#
# NOTE ON SCOPE. The Ace workspace root's .gitignore deliberately excludes ALL of
# Code/client-sites/ ("Real client/business data — NEVER ship, NEVER track"), because the
# distribution manifest is built from `git ls-files` and client work must never enter that payload.
# That exclusion is about the ACE payload, not about this client's own history — so this build keeps
# its own repo here, the same pattern already used by Code/web-mockup/desert-paws and
# alignwell-chiropractic. A repo at the workspace root would not capture this tree at all.

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# dependency trees (none committed; the gate scripts live in the skill, not here)
node_modules/

# never commit a real key or a local override
.mcp.json
.env
.env.*
*.pem

# The publish pipeline's own progress log. It is written AFTER `git add -A`, so it
# always lands one commit behind and shows the tree as dirty after every run. It is
# a transient run artifact -- nothing in the site or the gate stack reads it.
_audit/final-progress.txt

# rverify's per-page breakpoint captures. It writes <slug>-{desktop,laptop,tablet,mobile}.png
# for all 66 pages on every run -- ~290MB against a 110MB repo, regenerated from scratch each
# time and read by nothing downstream. The DETERMINISTIC evidence is the sibling
# <slug>.report.json (264KB total), which stays tracked. The P9 chrome-tournament captures in
# _audit/_renders/chrome/ and the two *-preview.png are real phase artifacts and stay tracked --
# these four suffixes match only rverify's output naming, so they cannot catch one by accident.
_audit/_renders/*-desktop.png
_audit/_renders/*-laptop.png
_audit/_renders/*-tablet.png
_audit/_renders/*-mobile.png
